&\text{Number of complete cycles: } \left\lfloor \frac{5000}{26} \right\rfloor + 1 = 192 \\
&\text{Remaining integers: } 5000 \mod 26 = 8 \\
&\text{The 8th integer in the sequence is } 8.
\end{align*}
$\boxed{8}$

